 ## Purpose
 
-The knowledge operation family module: the one `register_knowledge_tools(server, config)` that declares its family against the server it is handed and delegates every operation to the payload builders in `agents_remember.mcp.tools.knowledge`. It is "**appended** to `TOOL_REGISTRARS`, never inserted: FastMCP publishes tools in registration order, so every existing name keeps the position it was advertised at." It declares the five operation families "spelled as ``Doc13:181-187`` spells them" — `knowledge_read`, `knowledge_change`, `knowledge_diff`, `knowledge_integrity_check` and `knowledge_project`. **It deliberately performs no domain reasoning and mounts nothing for the reviewer**: "``KS-R22@v1`` owns the Intent Reviewer, the cockpit route and the browser client. What this module publishes is the interface L22 mounts -- the five operations, the review-matrix view and the typed models behind them -- and it adds no panel, no route and no client." It also holds no state, validates nothing itself and opens no dataset; the runtime configuration supplies it exactly one thing — "the workspace root a read falls back to when the caller names no repository of its own", handed over as the **default repository** rather than as half of a source-resolution pair — while "Everything else a handler needs -- the dataset path, the namespace and the destination -- is caller-supplied, because the substrate decides nothing about which dataset or which vault is meant."
+The knowledge operation family module: the one `register_knowledge_tools(server, config)` that declares its family against the server it is handed and delegates every operation to the payload builders in `agents_remember.mcp.tools.knowledge`. It is "**appended** to `TOOL_REGISTRARS`, never inserted: FastMCP publishes tools in registration order, so every existing name keeps the position it was advertised at." **On the held Source79 build it declares three operations: `knowledge_read`, `knowledge_diff` and `knowledge_integrity_check`,** through `_register_knowledge_read`, `_register_knowledge_diff` and `_register_knowledge_integrity_check`. **`knowledge_change` and `knowledge_project` are no longer registered** (MIK-R26 rule 5/Q4): the write plane is reached through the CLI file writer, and the mounted tool surface exposes no authoring writer and no projection renderer. It deliberately performs no domain reasoning, holds no state, validates nothing itself and opens no dataset; the runtime configuration supplies it the workspace root a read falls back to when the caller names no repository, and (since MIK-R23) the coordination root.
+
+**Historical (retired by MIK-R26).** The earlier five-operation description below — including the registrars for `knowledge_change` and `knowledge_project` and their dataset-selection routes — is retained as the record of the removed registrations; the current module's three registrars are those named above.
 
